  "digests": {
    "28": {
      "date": "2026-08-22",
      "edition": "Saturday 22 August",
      "sections": [
        {
          "kicker": "Tragic loss",
          "heading": "Fijian rugby player Saimoni Vunilagi dies in Japan of suspected heatstroke",
          "body": "Fijian rugby is mourning the tragic death of Saimoni Vunilagi, who has passed away in Japan at the age of 26. The back-row forward, who played for second-division professional side Kyushu KV, died in a Fukuoka hospital after suffering symptoms of severe heatstroke following a team training session. Kyushu KV, whom Vunilagi joined recently after beginning his professional career in 2023, released a statement saying they were \"devastated by this sudden news\" as they offered condolences to his family."
        }
      ]
    },
    "386": {
      "date": "2026-08-22",
      "edition": "Saturday 22 August",
      "sections": [
        {
          "kicker": "Squad contracts",
          "heading": "England stars Ollie Lawrence and Elliot Daly lose their central contracts",
          "body": "Steve Borthwick has made five changes to his 25-man central contracts list, omitting experienced backs Ollie Lawrence and Elliot Daly. The £150,000-a-year deals grant Borthwick greater control over his players ahead of next year's World Cup, but the omission of 33-year-old Daly and Bath centre Lawrence signals a major reshuffle. While Alex Coles and Sale prop Asher Opoku-Fordjour earn contracts, Ben Curry, Tom Roebuck and Tom Willis join Lawrence and Daly on the sidelines as Borthwick refines his plans."
        }
      ],
      "source": {
        "name": "Guardian Rugby Union"
      }
    },
    "387": {
      "date": "2026-08-22",
      "edition": "Saturday 22 August",
      "sections": [
        {
          "kicker": "Scrum-half rankings",
          "heading": "Maxime Lucu claims top spot as Antoine Dupont settles for bronze",
          "body": "France dominate the global scrum-half hierarchy, claiming three spots in Planet Rugby’s newly released top 10 rankings. Maxime Lucu takes the top spot as the game's most in-form number nine, leaving New Zealand's premier option in second while superstar Antoine Dupont settles for third place. La Rochelle’s Nolann Le Garrec also secures ninth place. Despite playing backup to both Dupont and Lucu internationally, Le Garrec’s trademark out-the-back passes and playmaking threat keep Les Bleus incredibly well-stocked at base."
        }
      ],
      "source": {
        "name": "Planet Rugby"
      }
    },
    "388": {
      "date": "2026-08-22",
      "edition": "Saturday 22 August",
      "sections": [
        {
          "kicker": "Injury blow",
          "heading": "Ireland lock Iain Henderson ruled out for months following hip surgery",
          "body": "Ireland and Ulster second row Iain Henderson will miss the start of the season after undergoing hip surgery, ruling him out for \"a number of months.\" The Ulster captain is one of four key players at the province undergoing surgical procedures. This prolonged absence severely disrupts Henderson's hopes of featuring in Ireland’s upcoming autumn matches, leaving the national side to look elsewhere for second-row depth as the international window approaches."
        }
      ],
      "source": {
        "name": "BBC Rugby Union"
      },
      "rung": "storyline"
    },
    "389": {
      "date": "2026-08-22",
      "edition": "Saturday 22 August",
      "sections": [
        {
          "kicker": "Fixture history",
          "heading": "Italy lost previous home clash against South Africa by 18 points",
          "body": "In their last meeting with South Africa, Italy suffered a 32-14 defeat at home during an international friendly in November 2025. That loss precedes a challenging campaign for the Azzurri, who sit 11th in the standings after losing all three of their opening matches. Italy have scored 37 points in their first three rounds, whilst conceding 131 points over the same period. This leaves the side with a points difference of minus 94. Their most recent outing in Round three ended in a heavy 10-57 defeat against Australia."
        }
      ],
      "rung": "data"
    },
    "390": {
      "date": "2026-08-22",
      "edition": "Saturday 22 August",
      "sections": [
        {
          "kicker": "Legal battle",
          "heading": "Scotland faces wider impact as rugby brain injury case proceeds to trial",
          "body": "The landmark legal battle over brain injuries in rugby has taken a major step forward, with the High Court ruling that hundreds of players have won their court battle for their claims to proceed to trial. The decision prevents the collapse of the case against rugby's governing bodies after previous applications threatened to strike out the vast majority of the claimants. With the lawsuit officially heading to trial, the wider sport now awaits the long-term implications of the ruling."
        }
      ],
      "source": {
        "name": "Guardian Rugby Union"
      },
      "rung": "storyline"
    },
    "391": {
      "date": "2026-08-22",
      "edition": "Saturday 22 August",
      "sections": [
        {
          "kicker": "Boardroom return",
          "heading": "Former captain Alun Wyn Jones joins Ospreys board amid survival fight",
          "body": "Former Wales captain Alun Wyn Jones has returned to Ospreys as a director with immediate effect. The 40-year-old former lock — who won 158 caps for Wales — joins the board at a turbulent time. Under Welsh Rugby Union proposals to cut to three professional men's sides, the region faces a direct battle against Scarlets for survival. Jones, who retired from playing in 2023, wants to \"help drive long-term growth and stability\" for the organisation."
        }
      ],
      "source": {
        "name": "BBC Rugby Union"
      }
    },
    "460": {
      "date": "2026-08-22",
      "edition": "Saturday 22 August",
      "sections": [
        {
          "kicker": "Tactical blueprint",
          "heading": "Kieran Read praises Argentina tactics as blueprint for New Zealand",
          "body": "Former New Zealand captain Kieran Read believes Argentina have handed the All Blacks a potential cheat code to unlock South Africa's rush defence. Despite Felipe Contepomi's men suffering a 17-10 defeat in Buenos Aires a fortnight ago, Read highlighted how Los Pumas successfully exposed the world champions on the edges with chips and cross-field kicks. Read urged the All Blacks to trust their depth and move the ball quickly, insisting that Argentina showed them 'exactly how we should try to beat the Springboks'."
        }
      ],
      "source": {
        "name": "SA Rugby Magazine"
      }
    },
    "461": {
      "date": "2026-08-22",
      "edition": "Saturday 22 August",
      "sections": [
        {
          "kicker": "Squad selection",
          "heading": "Joseph-Aukuso Suaalii and Len Ikitau return to Wallabies for Argentina tour",
          "body": "The Wallabies assemble in Sydney today before departing for Argentina, bolstered by the return of star midfielders Len Ikitau and Joseph-Aukuso Suaalii. Both have been cleared of injury to join Les Kiss’s 34-man squad for the upcoming two-Test tour. While Zane Nonggorr misses out through injury, the group remains largely settled following recent fixtures against Japan. Kiss noted he wants to \"maintain consistency in selection\" as the side prepares for a tough challenge against Los Pumas in San Salvador de Jujuy and Mendoza."
        }
      ],
      "source": {
        "name": "Planet Rugby"
      }
    },
    "463": {
      "date": "2026-08-22",
      "edition": "Saturday 22 August",
      "sections": [
        {
          "kicker": "Tragic loss",
          "heading": "Kyuden Voltex confirm Saimoni Vunilagi has died following suspected training heatstroke",
          "body": "The Japanese rugby community is in mourning after Kyushu Electric Power Kyuden Voltex announced the death of Saimoni Vunilagi on Saturday. The 26-year-old Fijian died of suspected heatstroke following a training session in Fukuoka. This tragedy highlights the extreme conditions currently facing players in Japan; Wallabies coach Les Kiss recently noted the \"physically taxing\" heat following his side's recent matches in the country. The loss of the Kyuden Voltex player has overshadowed the broader rugby landscape as the domestic game deals with this sudden tragedy."
        }
      ]
    },
    "465": {
      "date": "2026-08-22",
      "edition": "Saturday 22 August",
      "sections": [
        {
          "kicker": "Selection Call",
          "heading": "Dave Rennie hands Josh Moorby and Fabian Holland starts at Ellis Park",
          "body": "Head coach Dave Rennie has opted for \"X-factor\" over experience, naming Josh Moorby on the left wing and Fabian Holland at lock for Saturday's series opener against South Africa. Former fly-half Stephen Donald hailed Moorby’s inclusion as a \"wonderful story\" following the Hurricanes star’s rise through the NPC. Holland’s selection in the second row is the squad's biggest surprise after his recent return from a serious shoulder injury. New Zealand will reclaim the world No. 1 ranking with any victory today at Ellis Park."
